    "467": {
      "date": "2026-10-22",
      "edition": "Thursday 22 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury recovery",
          "heading": "Cheslin Kolbe still mending jaw broken in third All Blacks Test",
          "body": "Cheslin Kolbe has been mending a broken jaw since an All Blacks carrier's knee collided with it early in the third Test in Soweto, ending his game and delaying his Stormers homecoming. Speaking to former Springboks teammate Steven Kitshoff on For the Love of Rugby South Africa, Kolbe said: \"It's the most frustrating injury to have.\" It is the second time he has broken his jaw, and he was reduced to a liquid diet. He says he is finding a positive in more time with his family."
        },
